<title>DENMARK: Maersk adds new African service.</title>
<headline>Maersk adds new African service.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish shipping group A.P.Moeller said on Monday that its Maersk Line would open a new container service linking South Africa and Namibia with Europe and America.</p>
<p>From early in 1997 the service would offer sailings every two weeks of cellular vessels with large capacity for integral refrigerated containers, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Ships would call at ports in the Mediterranean, northern Europe, Scandinavia and the Baltic and link through Maersk's Spanish terminal to North and South America and the Middle East, it added.</p>
<p>-- Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
